# --- Test Case 4: Transpose Rewrite (Obvious Win) ---
#
# Expression: t(A %*% B) %*% C
#
# A = 1000x10
# B = 10x1000
# C = 1000x5
#
# --- Cost Analysis (FLOPs) ---
#
# Plan 1: Naive (No Rewrite)
#   1. T = (A %*% B)       (1000*10*1000 = 10,000,000 FLOPs) -> T is 1000x1000
#   2. U = t(T)            (Cost 0) -> U is 1000x1000
#   3. D = U %*% C         (1000*1000*5 = 5,000,000 FLOPs)
#   TOTAL (Plan 1) = 15,000,000 FLOPs
#
# Plan 2: Apply Rewrite -> (t(B) %*% t(A)) %*% C
#   Optimizer rewrites to a new chain: tB %*% tA %*% C
#   Dimensions: tB(1000x10), tA(10x1000), C(1000x5)
#
#   Sub-plan 2a: (tB %*% tA) %*% C
#     1. U = (tB %*% tA)     (1000*10*1000 = 10,000,000 FLOPs) -> U is 1000x1000
#     2. D = U %*% C         (1000*1000*5 = 5,000,000 FLOPs)
#     TOTAL (Sub-plan 2a) = 15,000,000 FLOPs
#
#   Sub-plan 2b: tB %*% (tA %*% C)
#     1. V = (tA %*% C)      (10*1000*5 = 50,000 FLOPs) -> V is 10x5
#     2. D = (tB %*% V)      (1000*10*5 = 50,000 FLOPs)
#     TOTAL (Sub-plan 2b) = 100,000 FLOPs  <- BEST
#
# We expect the optimizer to first apply the transpose rewrite,
# and then the matrix chain optimizer must find Sub-plan 2b.

A = rand(rows=1000, cols=10)
B = rand(rows=10, cols=1000)
C = rand(rows=1000, cols=5)

D = t(A %*% B) %*% C


print("Test Case 4 Complete. Result D (sum):")
print(sum(D))